## Problem
All pages in the SPA share the same `<title>` and `<meta name="description">` regardless of the current route.

## Current State
```html
<title>IT Operations - Knowledge Base</title>
<meta name="description" content="IT Operations Knowledge Base - QA Library" />
```

This is true for:
- Dashboard (/dashboard)
- Users (/users)
- Categories (/categories)
- QA Library (/qa)
- 404 page

## Required Fix
Update `<title>` and `<meta description>` dynamically in the `navigate()` function:
```javascript
function navigate(page) {
  const titles = {
    qa: 'QA Library - IT Operations KB',
    categories: 'Sub-Systems - IT Operations KB',
    users: 'Users - IT Operations KB',
    dashboard: 'Dashboard - IT Operations KB',
    '404': 'Page Not Found - IT Operations KB'
  };
  const descriptions = {
    qa: 'Browse and search QA entries for IT Operations',
    // ... etc
  };
  document.title = titles[page] || 'IT Operations - Knowledge Base';
  const desc = document.querySelector('meta[name="description"]');
  if (desc) desc.content = descriptions[page] || descriptions.qa;
}
```

## Priority: Low

## Problem
CSP `frame-ancestors 'self'` is set, which is correct for preventing clickjacking. However, the overall CSP could be reviewed for tightness.

## Current CSP
```
default-src 'self';
style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline';
font-src 'self';
img-src 'self' data:;
script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline';
base-uri 'self';
form-action 'self';
frame-ancestors 'self';
object-src 'none';
script-src-attr 'none';
upgrade-insecure-requests
```

## Observations
- `unsafe-inline` in style-src and script-src: acceptable for SPA but could be tightened with nonces
- `upgrade-insecure-requests`: good, forces HTTPS
- `form-action 'self'`: good, prevents form submission to external sites
- `frame-ancestors 'self'`: good, prevents clickjacking

## No immediate issues, but consider:
1. Adding `nonce` or `hash` to script-src for stricter CSP
2. Adding `report-uri` or `report-to` for CSP violation reporting

## Priority: Low
